Wayland: take BTN_* from <linux/input-event-codes.h>

wl_init.c includes <linux/input.h> for the BTN_* mouse button codes only,
which are Wayland protocol constants (the values wl_pointer.button carries).
QNX has no <linux/input.h>; the codes come with the
linux-headers-input-codes component as <linux/input-event-codes.h> --
the header wl_window.c already includes for the same purpose.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/src/wl_init.c
+++ b/src/wl_init.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <limits.h>
-#include <linux/input.h>
+#include <linux/input-event-codes.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
